# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# …except this one, deliberately.
#
# Android refuses to install a build over one signed with a different key, and
# Gradle's default debug key is generated per machine — so every CI run produced
# a signature the previous install rejected. Committing one fixed key makes
# every build installable over the last.
#
# It is not a secret and is not treated as one: it signs hand-installed builds
# only. An upload key for a store listing is a different key, belongs to
# whoever owns the listing, and must stay out of this repository.
!app/sudagri-debug.keystore
